gnome-shell-extension-zark (1.4-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Still reads the status files of zark 2.1.0 and later.
  * The extension in Spanish, and in Brazilian Portuguese, Portuguese,
    French, Italian, Catalan, Galician, German and Dutch: the menu, the
    details dialog, the notifications, the drive-gone dialog's title and
    first line, and the preferences follow the session's language.
    Commands and zark's own text stay in English, as zark writes them.
  * The catalogues are installed under /usr/share/locale; the package
    build-depends on gettext.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:56:30 +0100

gnome-shell-extension-zark (1.3-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * For zark 2.3.1; still reads the status files of zark 2.1.0 and later.
  * A dialog to close with OK when a running backup's drive goes away
    (zark 2.3.1's drive_gone): the drive's name, when it went away and
    zark's hint as written. Once per run and drive; a dialog closed by a
    screen lock comes back. A switch in the preferences, on by default.
  * While the drive is away, the menu's running backup and the drive's
    tab say when it went away.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:26:17 +0100

gnome-shell-extension-zark (1.2-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * For zark 2.3.0; still reads the status files of zark 2.1.0 and later.
  * The details dialog has an About tab: zark's mark, the installed zark's
    version (from dpkg's database, read without privileges), the
    extension's and GNOME Shell's versions, and Copy buttons for
    sudo zark status, sudo zark selftest, sudo zark backup and
    zark monitor (./zark for a zark not installed as a package).
  * A settings key, dpkg-status-path, for tests with an example file; the
    preferences' Development page says what each path is for.
  * The dark stylesheet is stylesheet-dark.css, so a change from the dark
    style to the light one takes effect at once.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:06:28 +0100

gnome-shell-extension-zark (1.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * GNOME Shell 51 (Ubuntu 26.10) as well as 50 (Ubuntu 26.04): the menu
    closes without animating before the details dialog opens, as on 50.
  * With /proc mounted hidepid, where root's processes cannot be seen, a
    run's missing pid no longer makes it orphaned: its heartbeat says
    running or stalled (orphan rule 4 of the status contract, as zark
    2.2 amends it; rules 3 and 5 unchanged).

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:58:00 +0100

gnome-shell-extension-zark (1.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * First release: the panel indicator and its menu, the details dialog
    (pools, datasets, backup drives and their points by month),
    notifications and preferences, read from the status files of zark 2.1.

 -- Juanmi Taboada <juanmi@juanmitaboada.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:05:00 +0100
